  "published": "2026-10-16T12:00:00Z",
  "summary": "Use-after-free through `init_using_cdict` and `init_using_ddict`",
  "details": "`CCtx::init_using_cdict` and `DCtx::init_using_ddict` (`experimental`\nfeature, deprecated) took the dictionary as `\u0026CDict\u003c'b\u003e` and `\u0026DDict\u003c'b\u003e`\nwith only `'b: 'a`, so the dictionary itself could be dropped while the\ncontext still pointed at it. The same mistake in other constructors was\nfixed earlier (\u003chttps://github.com/gyscos/zstd-rs/issues/365\u003e).\n\nThe flaw was corrected by taking `\u0026'a CDict\u003c'b\u003e` and `\u0026'a DDict\u003c'b\u003e`.",
